{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979683-gathering-the-cabal-you-all-meet-in-the-astral-reflection-of-a-14th-century-inn","id":979683,"title":"[Gathering the Cabal] You All Meet in the Astral Reflection of a 14th Century Inn","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-01T08:44:11-07:00","id":979683,"title":"[Gathering the Cabal] You All Meet in the Astral Reflection of a 14th Century Inn","content":"For some games, especially ones where the PC Mages have been established for some time, it's suitable to start a campaign with the latest Mystery intruding into their lives. I'm not asking about those.<br /> <br /> If there is a series of odd events which catalyses the Awakening of a half dozen Mages, or if you simply want to get a Cabal's worth of them together without relying on orders from the Concillium, what methods have you used to get the gang together? Particularly as a group who have Awakened at about the same time are likely to fracture if they are picked up by the Orders for training.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/528-darth-fanboy","name":"Darth Fanboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar528_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T11:00:45-07:00","id":979759,"title":"","content":"It depends on how many players are in the game, their Paths, etc. Generally speaking, though, having the PCs meet isn't enough to have them stick together; for that, they need common purpose and a chance to build mutual trust.<br /> <br /> For that reason, giving them a mutual Obsession or reason for alliances of mutual protection are probably the best ways to start things off. Preferably both. I've seen an Acanthus be led by visions to find the other PCs, but that mutual binding only worked because they were the <i>only</i> three Awakened (so far as they knew) in their small, sleepy town. One of their first activities was to build a sanctum together, where they could mutually work their magic, and thus trust began to be established. If they were in a large city, though, they'd likely never have met nor cared to meet.<br /> <br /> Also important is to have all the PCs share a mutual connection. It can't be &quot;Odin knows Boudica knows Amon&quot;. Otherwise, the party won't bond effectively and mistrust will flow between unknowns.<br /> <br /> These things don't have to be <i>big</i> either; just something to start with. Like, say, the trio of Awakened all want to get rich somehow, without drawing <i>too</i> much attention to themselves. The Moros gathers start-up capital, the Obrimos creates a business, the Acanthus ensures it gets customers. They might not even need Awakened skill for that one. Far less obvious and less likely to draw the attention of rivals than winning big on the horses or at a casino.<br /> <br /> Or perhaps each member of the cabal has access to something the other wants and is willing to give it more cheaply than someone else. Access to rotes can draw hefty costs, but if you just so happen to have a grimoire-heavy cabal-mate who really enjoys prostitutes and you just so happen to run or know someone who runs a brothel, well... An arrangement is easier to come to terms with.<br /> <br /> I'm just spitballing now because this is a genuinely difficult part of game design. Trust can be assumed far more easily than built. Thanks for getting me thinking about this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T17:16:46-07:00","id":979945,"title":"","content":"On a slightly less impressive note, and to be honest based on how it's been going so far I'm not 100% sure I recommend it, but you can have a political fiat from the Hierarch. In my game the Free Council are largely in charge and to encourage communion of ideas there's a Silver Law stating that those who Awaken in close proximity to one another (within a year or so) must form a Cabal for a time, though they can break away later. They are then commonly given grunt-work tasks to foster team-building. There's <i>always </i>a crisis around somewhere. This is not terribly dissimilar to how Dave managed it in Broken Diamond as I recall.<br /> <br /> Or you could do what my first Storyteller did which is that the Cabal formation is part of a prophecy that the Pentacle would like to see fulfilled, and immediately attention is paid to the PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12121-ainsoph","name":"AinSoph","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T21:43:18-07:00","id":980073,"title":"","content":"I've run two chronicles and currently planning my third. For the first one I united the cabal by giving them a common threat, as newly Awakened they were all targeted by the same false friend and come together to fight back. For my second I used a mentor figure who originally found them as newly Awakened, gave them their initial training together and introduced them to Awakened society. For my upcoming chronicle they will be linked by a common mystery, namely waking up together near the woods with no memory of how they got there, followed by independently finding evidence that in spite of having no memory of it they did/do know each other. What's more their little group of forgotten friends included two more people that investigating uncovers disappeared on the same night the characters woke up near the woods only those two never returned.<br /> \u200bYou can also throw them straight into the flak, you work together not because anything ties you to each other, but simply because you have no hope of surviving alone and you know everyone else is the enemy.<br /> \u200bAlso, pre-Awakened ties will still exist. When surrounded by the new and the strange people who barely knew your name will still feel more tied to you then anything else. In real life common experience and history are often the base of new friendships.<br /> \u200bYou can, if all else fails, tell them they all got drunk and woke up with a hangover and apparently a new cabal. All registered with the Consillium and everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6084,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","user":"2ptTakrill","date":". 10-02-2016, 12:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T04:40:06-07:00","id":980192,"title":"","content":"I think the easiest way to gather a cabal of new mages is to have their first teachers from their orders dump them off somewhere with a comment of &quot;okay good now you need to learn the other lessons of being a mage the stuff I can't teach you. The stuff you will learn here, like how to work with other mages of other paths and orders who are peers. Good luck.&quot; Out comes an bald man in a wheel chair he looks at you and says &quot;Hello [Your Shadow Name Here] I am Professor [Fill in name here], this is my college. We offer Associates and bachelor degrees in business, culinary arts, computers sciences, and paralegal degrees. We also will help you make your place in the society of mages.&quot;<br /> <br /> Another one is based around my experiences.<br /> A letter arrives for you, when you open it it is instructions from the Consillium to go to a specific place at a specific time to meet with the mages you have been assigned to form a Cabal. They took great care to pair you all up. Either that or some Arcanths jerk pumped a bunch of fate magic into some darts and threw them at your pictures to see who would get assigned to be partners, or maybe you pissed off what ever supernal entity they asked to make these teams up. Either way your sure careful planning, forethought, logic, and attempts at sober thinking were not involved in the formation of this cabal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T06:19:58-07:00","id":980212,"title":"","content":"I really think it is the players responsobility to decide why they formed a cabal (unless it is part of the plot). The making of the cabal should really be part of the character creation process.<br /> The players should define two aspects of the relationship between two (or more) PCs.<br /> If the group really needs help founding a cabal there is always problem A, the councilium/heiarch/assembly/exarchs aska for volonteers to form a cabal until problem A is resolved. So when the players solve problem A the characters have the options of going back to their original cabals or forming a new cabal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7463-toine","name":"Toine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7463_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T11:43:11-07:00","id":980361,"title":"","content":"The Mage Noir game I played in started with the PCs being interrogated by the city's Sentinel about the murder of a Seer, because Time magic had revealed we were all involved somehow, despite most of us not knowing each other or the victim. Naturally we all started investigating, thus getting involved. \ud83d\ude09","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T00:28:04-07:00","id":980627,"title":"","content":"Random Note: I now really want to start a game in the astral reflection of a 14th century inn, or perhaps reunite a cabal after a long period of downtime in one.(The Astral as a safe meeting place is something I haven't ever explored)<br /> <br /> Slightly Pertinent Note: In the one mage game I ran, the players awakenings were each tied into the same mystery (The subtle opening gambits of a power struggle between 5 different mage factions.) I gave each player a free couple of dots of the Destiny Merit (this was 1st ed) and gave them a shared fate. Under fate sight mages would see the bonds of destiny between the PCs and encourage them to stay together. <br /> <br /> A little more heavy handed than I would normally like, but it led straight into the central plot of the story and really gave my very diverse PCs strong reasons to interact and work together to find out what had happened to them. Consider some kind of Mystery or conspiracy that your characters can share and work together on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T03:10:07-07:00","id":980683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darth Fanboy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979683-gathering-the-cabal-you-all-meet-in-the-astral-reflection-of-a-14th-century-inn#post979683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If there is a series of odd events which catalyses the Awakening of a half dozen Mages, or if you simply want to get a Cabal's worth of them together without relying on orders from the Concillium, what methods have you used to get the gang together? Particularly as a group who have Awakened at about the same time are likely to fracture if they are picked up by the Orders for training.</div> </div> </div> </div>That last sentence doesn't have to be true. Firstly, the Pentacle are an alliance; they can violently disagree, but ultimately they broadly accept the others right to exist in the same society. In fact, there seems a basic bias in the Pentacle in favour of multi-order cabals. Assuming any mentors are fairly reasonable, they'll want to encourage these new awakened to form a cabal.<br /> Secondly, (and Sanctum and Sigil goes into quite dry detail about this); a cabal isn't really a group of friends. It's fundamentally the lowest level of the Pentacle legal system. The cabal is there to police it's own members as much as it's meant to be an outward facing alliance. Therefore, it's quite possible for magi who disagree quite deeply to work together on that basis. A Guardian and a Libertine can be part of the same cabal precisely because they don't really trust each other; the cabal is there to allow them to monitor and police each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}